<https://ontology.pointonezero.com/strategy/apqc/banking> a owl:Ontology ;
    dct:title "P1Z Industry Overlay: APQC Banking PCF" ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" ;
    dct:source "APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF), Banking, Excel Version 8.0" ;
    dct:description "Banking industry overlay module: a separate module importing the cross-industry spine (PCF v8.0, spine v0.3.0, core v0.4.0). Adds and specializes only, never redefines a core or spine term: industry-new process elements (with parentProcess links into the spine or this overlay) and industry-new metrics with their cross-maps. Shared elements and metrics remain asserted solely by the spine and cross-industry metrics files. Version-skew editorial differences observed in the industry workbook (label case changes, metric text polish, coarser metric placements) are deliberately not asserted; the cross-industry v8.0 files are canonical for shared content." ;
    dct:rights "APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) is an open standard developed by APQC, a nonprofit that promotes benchmarking and best practices worldwide. The PCF is intended to facilitate organizational improvement through process management and benchmarking, regardless of industry, size, or geography. To download the full PCF or industry-specific versions of the PCF, as well as associated measures and benchmarking, please visit www.apqc.org/pcf." .

# Industry-new process elements (114, levels 1-4)

apqc:PCF14018 a p1z:Process ;
    skos:prefLabel "Integrate channels" ;
    p1z:apqcId "14018" ;
    p1z:apqcHierarchyId "3.2.5.2" ;
    p1z:apqcLevel 4 ;
    p1z:metricsAvailable false ;
    p1z:parentProcess apqc:PCF20006 .

apqc:PCF14020 a p1z:Process ;
    skos:prefLabel "Perform data acquisition and storage" ;
    p1z:apqcId "14020" ;
